# Media Workbench v2 — screen comp: Runs with live run-queue rail (conventional list + Instrument-Deck-derived rail, macOS light appearance)
# Note: the rail borrows Instrument Deck's *queue rail idea only*. The prompt deliberately avoids
# "instrument", "deck", "console" and "studio" wording — in v1 that vocabulary hijacked the render into a synthesiser.
schema: "0.4"
id: mw-screen-runs-rail
type: image
service: gemini
model: gemini-3.1-flash-image
quality: high
prompt:
  text: |
    A straight-on screenshot of a macOS 14 Sonoma app window, light system appearance, SF Pro type, traffic lights, unified toolbar titled "Runs" with a segmented filter "All | Running | Failed" and a search field. The app is a media-generation workbench; this screen lists generation runs and shows the live job queue.

    Left: the translucent source-list sidebar: "Requests 3", "Library", "Runs" (selected) with a small blue badge "2", "Styles", divider, "Settings".

    Centre: a native table of past runs with small image thumbnails at row start. Columns: "Run", "Provider", "Attempts", "Grade", "When". Rows:
    "pricing-hero · gemini-3.1-flash-image · 3/4 · 84 · now";
    "og-card · grok-2-image · 2/2 · 91 · 4m";
    "changelog-banner · qwen-image · 1/1 · 58 · 1h" (grade in a small red pill);
    "onboarding-spot · gemini-3.1-flash-image · 3/3 · 88 · 2h";
    "team-photo-bg · qwen-image · 0/2 · failed · 3h" (small red "failed" pill).
    Grades sit in small pills, green when passed, red when failed, grey when ungraded. One row also shows a tiny override glyph next to its grade.

    Right: a narrow vertical queue rail (about 300pt) titled "Queue", plain white rows separated by hairlines. Each job row: run name, provider, a thin horizontal progress bar, elapsed time, and a small circular "×" cancel button:
    "pricing-hero · gemini · attempt 4/4 · 62% · 0:48";
    "og-card ×2 · grok · 1/2 · 20% · 0:12";
    "hero-alt · qwen-image · queued".
    At the rail bottom a muted caption "Keeps running if window closes" and a small hint "⌘. cancel".

    Plain, native list UI with live progress. Short legible labels and numbers only.
  negative: >
    garbled text, lorem ipsum, watermark, mobile frame, browser chrome, Windows UI,
    perspective tilt, synthesizer/audio-hardware look, CAD tool, manuscript editor,
    knobs, faders, sliders, VU meters, waveform, mixing console, LED displays, rack hardware,
    dark mode, terminal window, emoji icons
  style: "UI design screen comp, straight-on screenshot framing, no perspective, no camera tilt, crisp pixel-sharp interface"
output:
  formats:
    - format: png
      quality: 95
  dimensions:
    width: 2560
    height: 1600
    aspect_ratio: "16:10"
eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.7
  criteria:
    depicts_the_product:
      weight: 0.4
      description: "reads as a media-generation request/review/grading tool, specifically a history of generation runs with a live queue of in-flight image generations"
    follows_spec:
      weight: 0.35
      description: "shows (1) a runs table with provider/model, attempts and gate-coloured grade pills; (2) a right-hand queue rail with per-job progress bars, elapsed time and cancel; (3) a queued job alongside running ones; (4) the source-list sidebar with Runs selected and a running-count badge"
    macos_native:
      weight: 0.25
      description: "reads as a native macOS 14 light-appearance window with source list, table, toolbar filter and search"
  reject_if:
    - depicts a different product category (audio workstation, synthesiser, CAD tool, manuscript editor, web page)
    - primary labels (Queue, run names, percentages) are unreadable or garbled
tags: [screen-comp, macos, media-workbench, v2]
